---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Terms of use — Hours Apart';
const description = 'Terms for using Hours Apart, the world clock and meeting-planning tools.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/terms">
  <article class="max-w-2xl">
    <header class="mb-7">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-paper-700">
        These terms describe the basic rules for using Hours Apart. By using the site, you agree to
        them.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Using the service</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        Hours Apart provides world-clock, daylight-saving and meeting-planning tools for general
        informational use. You may use the site lawfully for personal or business planning. Do not
        interfere with the site, attempt to gain unauthorised access, or use automated requests in a
        way that harms its availability for others.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Time and daylight-saving information</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        We aim to make the information useful and accurate, but time-zone rules, daylight-saving
        changes and local observance can change. Check important appointments, travel plans and
        legal or financial deadlines against an appropriate authoritative source. The service is
        provided as-is and without a guarantee that it will always be available or error-free.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Third-party services and advertising</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        The site may link to or use third-party services, including calendar providers, Tally for
        feedback and Google AdSense for advertising. Their services are governed by their own terms
        and privacy policies. Our use of advertising technology is described in our
        <a
          href="/privacy"
          class="ring-focus rounded font-medium text-paper-900 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-paper-700"
          >Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        We may update the site and these terms as the service develops. Continued use after an
        update means you accept the updated terms. To report a problem or send feedback, use the
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="ring-focus rounded font-medium text-paper-900 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-paper-700"
          >contact page</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="ring-focus rounded text-sm font-medium text-paper-900 hover:text-paper-700"
      >
        &larr; Back to the world clock
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
